    <!-- Widgets screen -->
    <string name="widgets_intro">Three widgets: bar, ring and mini. Each one has its own theme and background opacity, independent of the phone\'s theme.</string>
    <string name="widgets_defaults">Default look</string>
    <string name="widgets_defaults_desc">Used for new widgets. Any widget can be adjusted on its own: long-press it → Settings.</string>
    <string name="widgets_apply_all">Apply to all widgets</string>
    <string name="widgets_how">How to add</string>
    <string name="how_bar_title">Bar 5×1</string>
    <string name="how_bar_text">Long-press an empty spot on the home screen → Widgets → EcoWi → Bar. To make a stack, drop it onto another widget of the same size. 5×1 needs a 5-column grid (Home screen settings → Grid).</string>
    <string name="how_ring_title">Ring</string>
    <string name="how_ring_text">A 2×2 circular gauge. Stretch it to 4×2 to see this phone\'s battery next to it, like the Battery widget.</string>
    <string name="how_lock_title">Lock screen</string>
    <string name="how_lock_text">Mini is marked as a lock-screen widget. If your One UI version allows third-party widgets there, look for EcoWi in the list. If not, the Now Bar shows the charge on the lock screen.</string>
    <string name="how_nowbar_title">Now Bar</string>
    <string name="how_nowbar_text">Turn on Live mode in Alerts — the charge appears in the Now Bar and status bar (Android 16 / One UI 8). If EcoWi doesn\'t show up there, enable Live notifications for all apps in Developer options.</string>

